.Dd February 11, 2026
.Dt CPIO 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cpio
.Nd copy file archives in and out
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl o
.Op Fl v
.Op Fl H Ar format
.Op Fl F Ar archive
.Op Fl R Ar uid:gid
.Nm
.Fl i
.Op Fl t
.Op Fl v
.Op Fl dmu
.Op Fl H Ar format
.Op Fl F Ar archive
.Op Fl -safe-extract
.Op Fl -no-absolute-paths
.Op Fl -no-overwrite
.Op Fl -numeric-owner
.Nm
.Fl p
.Op Fl v
.Op Fl dmu
.Ar directory
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility reads and writes cpio archives using copy-out
.Pq Fl o ,
copy-in
.Pq Fl i ,
and pass-through
.Pq Fl p
modes.
.Pp
Pathnames for
.Fl o
and
.Fl p
are read from standard input, one per line.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl o
Create archive.
.It Fl i
Extract archive.
.It Fl p
Pass-through copy to directory.
.It Fl F Ar archive
Read/write archive file instead of stdin/stdout.
.It Fl H Ar format
Archive format: bin, odc, newc.
.It Fl t
Table of contents only.
.It Fl v
Verbose output.
.It Fl d
Create leading directories.
.It Fl m
Preserve modification time on extraction/copy.
.It Fl u
Allow overwrite behavior (accepted for compatibility).
.It Fl R Ar uid:gid
Set owner fields while writing archive.
.It Fl -safe-extract
Reject absolute and parent-traversal path entries.
.It Fl -no-absolute-paths
Reject absolute path entries during extraction.
.It Fl -no-overwrite
Do not replace existing files on extraction.
.It Fl -numeric-owner
Apply numeric owner/group on extraction (root only).
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
Success.
.It 1
Non-fatal errors occurred (partial success).
.It 2
Fatal error.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pax 1
.Sh STANDARDS
Behavior follows POSIX cpio model with pragmatic safety extensions.
